By 

	Todd Spangler

NY Digital Editor

Are TV broadcasters obligated to carry the U.S. president’s comments live on their government-licensed airwaves? The current head of the FCC indicated that he believes they are.

Brendan Carr, the Trump-appointed chairman of the FCC, said Wednesday that the agency will consider ABC‘s decision to not carry a live broadcast of President Donald Trump‘s July 16 speech about U.S. election security as part of its early review of licenses to eight ABC-owned stations.








